{"id":"chatcmpl-4ed0fbfb-8f8d-4a08-8093-46fca3b2fc95","object":"chat.completion","created":1795250687,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task shows a robust pattern for resolving ambiguous visual findings when the imaging view (lateral) makes side-specific localization inherently difficult. The successful strategy combined multiple independent model assessments, explicitly tracked disagreement, and used a verifier to flag likely side-assignment errors before committing to an answer. The key insight is that when the view type undermines the discriminative feature, cross-model consensus plus a risk-aware verification step outperforms any single model's output.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When the imaging view or data format makes the target feature ambiguous, first identify the view/format limitation, then gather multiple independent assessments rather than trusting one model.\",\n    \"Explicitly track and surface model disagreement as a risk signal; disagreement on a side-specific or localization task is a cue to invoke a verification step rather than average or pick arbitrarily.\",\n    \"Use a verifier to check for systematic error modes (e.g., side-assignment errors, left/right confusion) that are plausible given the view or data constraints, and let that risk assessment override a single confident model.\",\n    \"Anchor interpretation on known anatomical priors (e.g., normal asymmetry baselines) and assess deviation from that baseline rather than absolute position, especially when the view compresses or overlaps structures.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"medical_imaging_QA\": \"Identify view/format limitations first; collect 2-4 independent model reads; treat disagreement as a trigger for verification, not a nuisance.\",\n    \"ambiguous_localization_tasks\": \"When left/right or side assignment is hard due to view overlap, explicitly ask models about side-assignment risk and prefer the answer consistent with anatomical priors plus verifier risk flags.\",\n    \"multi_model_consensus\": \"Log each model's answer and rationale; use a verifier to adjudicate conflicts by naming the likely error mode, then commit to the answer that survives that scrutiny.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Before answering, confirm the view/format and whether it makes the target feature (e.g., side-specific elevation) ambiguous; if so, require multiple independent assessments.\",\n    \"Before finalizing, run a verification step that names the most plausible error mode (e.g., side-assignment error) and check whether the proposed answer is consistent with anatomical priors and the verifier's risk flag.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":690,"total_tokens":1180,"completion_tokens":490,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":690},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":490}}}